# SRG-APP-000435-WSR-000148  -  CAT II
# The web server must be tuned to handle the operational requirements of the
# hosted application.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000435-WSR-000148
group:           V-206433
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-002385
control_rev5:    SC-5

contribution:    Splunk can cap simultaneous HTTP connections, HTTP worker threads and
                 concurrent searches on each of its listeners so that normal traffic cannot
                 exhaust the instance, while the magnitudes themselves come from the site's
                 expected traffic.

governs:         inputs.conf - Configures inputs, distributed inputs such as forwarders, and file system
                 monitoring.
governs:         limits.conf - Limits on how much work searches and data processing may consume.
governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] maxSockets min 0
check:           web.conf [settings] maxThreads min 0
check:           server.conf [httpServer] maxSockets min 0
check:           server.conf [httpServer] maxThreads min 0
check:           inputs.conf [http] maxSockets min 0
check:           inputs.conf [http] maxThreads min 0
check:           server.conf [httpServer] streamInWriteTimeout min 1
check:           limits.conf [search] base_max_searches present
check:           limits.conf [search] max_searches_per_cpu present
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          server.conf [httpServer] maxSockets https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
vendor:          server.conf [httpServer] maxThreads https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] maxSockets https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] maxThreads https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Expected user traffic and the risk analysis documents that set the limit
                 magnitudes, which are organizational determinations the check text calls
                 for
external:        Operating system file descriptor and process limits (ulimit, or systemd
                 LimitNOFILE and LimitNPROC), which bound what the application limits can
                 reach
external:        Host CPU and memory sizing, since the automatic limits are derived from
                 estimated server capacity
external:        Any front-end load balancer or reverse proxy performing rate limiting or
                 connection shaping

citation:        SRG-APP-000435-WSR-000148 check text; web.conf.spec:1098-1113;
                 server.conf.spec:1362-1402; inputs.conf.spec:1683-1706;
                 limits.conf.spec:445-464
finding:         Splunk accepts HTTP connections, worker threads or concurrent searches
                 without an enforced limit on at least one listener (a negative maxSockets
                 or maxThreads value in web.conf, server.conf or inputs.conf), so ordinary
                 traffic can exhaust the instance.
